Q: gcc 13.3.0: [-Wstringop-overflow=] A: <p>Like <a href="https://stackoverflow.com/a/79868584/2410359">@3CEZVQ</a> good answer, yet with a different take on detection and handing.</p>
<hr />
<p><code>ssize_t read(size_t count; int fd, void buf[count], size_t count);</code> expects a <code>size_z count</code>.  <code>size_t</code> is an <em>unsigned type</em>.</p>
<p>OP's code is using <code>fi.st_size</code> which is a <em>signed</em> type.</p>
<p>Warning is about using an out-of-range value for <code>count</code>.</p>
<pre><code>if (fi.st_size &lt; 0 || fi.st_size &gt;= SIZE_MAX || fi.st_size &gt;= SSIZE_MAX) {
  ;  // Handle trouble with TBD_code
} else {
  size_t sz = (size_t) fi.st_size;
  htt = calloc(1, sz + 1);
  r = read(fd, htt, sz);
  ...
}
</code></pre>

